            "label": "T2: Playing computer games",
            "text": "#Q Discuss the effects of computer games on children's behavior and what can be done to minimize the bad effects.\n\n#A Nowadays, playing computer games has become more and more common among children. While some people think that computer games help children learn useful skills, others argue that they have a bad influence on children's behaviour. This essay will discuss the effects of computer games on children's behaviour and some solutions to minimise the bad effects.\n\n#A Although some games can improve children's problem-solving skills, there are several negative effects of computer games on children's behaviour. One main effect is that violent games can make children more aggressive. This is because children often copy what they see, and in some games, players have to fight or kill to win. For example, a child who plays shooting games for hours may get angry easily and hit other children at school. In addition, another effect is that children may become addicted to games. As a result, they spend less time studying, doing exercise and talking with their family and friends.\n\n#A To deal with this problem, there are some effective solutions to minimise the bad effects. One main solution is that parents should control the time and the type of games their children play. For instance, they can allow their children to play for only one hour a day and choose games that are suitable for their age. This may help children build good habits from an early age. Another solution is that schools should organise more outdoor and group activities. Therefore, children will have other interesting things to do and will spend less time in front of the screen.\n\n#A In conclusion, computer games can make children more aggressive and addicted, which badly affects their behaviour. However, if parents and schools work together to control playing time and offer more healthy activities, these bad effects can be greatly reduced."
